  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ebafb35eac131f04aa192af6e919cd2d, type: 3}
  m_Name: Glossary_Shockley
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PNJunctionLab.GlossaryTopic
  topicId: shockley
  title: Shockley I-V Law
  summary: I = Is * (exp(V / (n * VT)) - 1), with VT = kT/q (~25.9 mV at 300 K) and n = 1..2. Forward voltage drops ~2 mV/C as temperature rises; reverse Is grows with temperature.
  explanationLine: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 00e887df8a2ea4f4e85f565097e9c167, type: 2}
